+\subsection{Status of the research questions}
+For RQ1, no acceptance or preservation failures were observed among the four evaluated patches. This provides no characterization of failure patterns on a broader task set. For RQ2 and RQ3, one session per condition on a single development task is insufficient to support comparative effect estimates. The recorded times remain descriptive; they establish no layout or package cost advantage.
+
+The next evidence needed is qualification and pilot coverage beyond the history-filter workflow, followed by a frozen main task set and analysis plan. Proposed admin filtering, display-name editing, and session revocation remain unrun pilot candidates. No main-study effect estimate, interval, or hypothesis test is reported here.
